WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.319
Marvel's two Guardians of the Galaxy installments
are action-packed, exciting, and even meaningful.

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:07.329
Best of all, they're really funny.

00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:11.140
Usually that humor is intentional, but sometimes,
it's a complete accident.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.950
Which is great, because these bloopers make
us love Guardians of the Galaxy even more.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.530
Rooker books it

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.970
You think walking and chewing gum at the same
time is hard?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.100
Trying walking and talking!

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.750
Sure, it sounds like something you do every
day, but as actors Michael Rooker and Tom

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.220
Proctor prove here, it's not always as easy
as it seems.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.460
"He was cargo!

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.860
And you're always going soft on him!"

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:32.960
"And you!

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.220
Walked us right off the set!"

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.020
"Yes, I did!

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.720
And I'm gonna do it again."

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.800
A blooper from a galaxy far, far away

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.890
Kurt Russell is a living legend, but even
legends sometimes screw up their lines.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.079
Like in this blooper, where Russell accidentally
gives a shout out to the franchise that inspired

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:50.620
much of the space action in Guardians of the
Galaxy.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.010
"Well, even where I reside out past the edge
of what's known, we've heard tell about the

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.120
man they call Star Wars."

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.420
"We could be in trouble."

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.079
Dance-off in space

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:06.860
In the theatrical ending to the first film,
Chris Pratt's Star-Lord uses the threat of

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.680
a dance off as a diversion.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.330
But in this awesome outtake, Lee Pace's bad
guy Ronan the Accuser accepts the challenge,

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.580
leading to the epic showdown we've all been
waiting for.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.320
"It's on!"

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.650
Wire work gone haywire

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:30.740
The Guardians of the Galaxy movies take place
on various planets with varying levels of

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:31.740
gravity.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.869
To make it look realistic, the actors have
to strap themselves in for some wire work.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:37.450
Sometimes the results are amazing.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.940
And other times, this happens.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.000
"I think we got it."

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.460
Rocket to the gag reel

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.040
Groot and Rocket Raccoon are the result of
the combined magic of CGI, the voice work

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.520
of stars Vin Diesel and Bradley Cooper, and
motion capture.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.659
And thank goodness the movies used real-life
human stand-ins for the tree man and his trash

00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:03.729
panda buddy, because how else would a blooper
featuring these two characters even be possible?

00:02:03.729 --> 00:02:06.320
"I told you, you can't fit!"

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.200
"Rrrrgh!"

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.340
"Cut!"

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.519
Nonsense!

00:02:15.519 --> 00:02:18.819
Here's a blooper-stuffed take that made its
way into the final cut of Guardians of the

00:02:18.819 --> 00:02:19.819
Galaxy.

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:23.969
While dealing with a rare goods dealer known
as the Broker, Yondu frustrates and upsets

00:02:23.969 --> 00:02:25.980
the guy by mumbling a bunch of gibberish.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.051
It's a little more than co-star Sea Gunn could
handle, and director James Gunn kept the result

00:02:30.051 --> 00:02:31.051
in the film.

00:02:31.051 --> 00:02:32.051
"The high-end…"

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.051
*babbles*

00:02:33.051 --> 00:02:34.540
"It's a tight-knit…"

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.540
*babbles*

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.700
"The high-end community is a tight-knit…!"

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.939
More nonsense!

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:45.659
It's apparently no sweat for Michael Rooker
to make up his own real-sounding nonsense

00:02:45.659 --> 00:02:46.859
words in a pinch.

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:51.489
But give the guy some comic book/science-fiction
movie dialogue heavy on the technical side,

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:53.680
and he just can't get the words out without
stumbling.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.680
Whoops!

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.340
"Craglin, we need an extraction at…

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.240
UGH!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.480
Quadrant.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.880
Haha."

00:03:01.049 --> 00:03:03.240
Lee Pace loses his place

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:08.189
Prior to joining the Marvel Cinematic Universe,
Lee Pace worked primarily an actor in more

00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:09.879
straightforward dramas.

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:13.949
Those roles didn't necessarily prepare him
for the bonkers role of Ronan the Accuser,

00:03:13.949 --> 00:03:16.939
as this blooper of Pace struggling to nail
the role shows.

00:03:16.939 --> 00:03:20.159
"Wait, one more time, what was that?

00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:23.099
There, and then turn?"

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:24.709
"POWER!

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:26.530
Becomes the only law!

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.810
Wait, that's not right, is it?"

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.150
Chris Pratt doinks around

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.469
Finally, the encounter between the Guardians
of the Galaxy and the alien ruler Ayesha drives

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:37.129
much of the conflict in the second film.

00:03:37.129 --> 00:03:41.280
But it could have all gone very differently
if Star-Lord had gotten his way.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.400
He didn't, but at least the effort left us
with this amazing gem.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:52.999
"I personally control half the DNA by doing
something I call doinking."

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.329
"Hahah!"

00:03:54.329 --> 00:03:55.329
Thanks for watching!

00:03:55.329 --> 00:03:57.439
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:57.439 --> 00:03:59.540
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

